## Per-stratum resolve rates

$stratum_table

Intervals are Wilson score intervals at 95 percent. An empty cell is reported
as (0.00, 1.00): no evidence, not a measured zero.

## Paired comparisons

$mcnemar_table

Exact binomial McNemar on the discordant pairs. The design is within-subject,
so the unpaired chi-square would be the wrong test. Each attempt, one
instance under one worker with one seed, contributes its own pair: a second
seed or a second worker on the same instance is never collapsed into the
first, so both are counted rather than one silently overwriting the other.

## Cost

$cost_table

Cost is reported as WALL CLOCK, the real cost axis in this configuration: the
brain is a rate-limited subscription CLI, not metered per token. Total wall
clock and wall clock per RESOLVED task are reported per condition. A
condition that resolves nothing shows an infinite wall clock per resolved
task, because zero or any finite number would read as free.

